{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfcw9yH75CedcTngr1ZsD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate for this slot (refining the incumbent), and it passes the self-check: `OK`. Its smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was −3489.8, against the incumbent's −3531.2. That gap isn't a real comparison yet, because the smoke fit is one chain of 100 draws. The same fit's PSIS-LOO estimate is also flagged unreliable: 6.2% of trials have Pareto k > 0.5, against a 1% tolerance. A short fit like this may just be noisy, but admission's full fit has to clear that too, and so far nothing I ran checks it.\n\n**Name:** `asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch`\n\n**Change:** I kept all of `most_lopsided_stretch_aversion` and made one stated change, taken from the rank-1 model `run_variety_asymmetric_ideal_rate`. Switching more often than a person's ideal rate now costs only a shared, fitted fraction (`over_frac = exp(log_over)`, prior on `log_over` ~ Normal(0, 1)) of what the same shortfall in switching costs. The two models' best extra cues (the most lopsided stretch, and the asymmetric tolerance) both target the high-alternation discrepancy. Each has only been tested on its own base model, so this tests whether they stack.\n\n**Why not a side bias:** I didn't address this round's critique. Its two findings are a left/right response bias and person-to-person spread in that bias, and neither survives the FDR correction (q = 0.14 and 0.18). The run-length-variety base gained about 47 nats when the asymmetric tolerance was added to it, while an earlier side-bias model was pruned 135 nats behind. The other slot refining the incumbent may well take the side-bias route anyway.\n\n**Not checked yet:**\n- **Novelty:** whether the predictions differ enough from the incumbent's and the rank-1 model's to pass the novelty gate.\n- **Convergence:** a single chain can't report R-hat, so admission's full fit is the first real test of convergence and speed. The smoke fit took 108 s.\n\nAll three files are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_4/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2359,"cache_read_input_tokens":76292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2359,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9193276b-5fff-4fb0-a9c4-2a0d91a6bf80","uuid":"a514778c-e7d4-4833-80ab-a1cd4504f437","timestamp":"2026-10-02T06:26:34.246Z","request_id":"req_011Cfcw9xsYyRMsF1gTdzNeT"}
